During project implementation the M4EG network will increase to 350 local authorities, and 12 local authorities will go through a process of portfolio development. Three funding facilities will be available to the local authorities in the network: the EU Project Fund (2021), Annual Portfolio Call (2021-2023) and M4EG Innovation Project Call (2021-2023).

Duties and Responsibilities

Working under the overall guidance and supervision of the Regional Project Manager and the direct supervision of UNDP Moldova Portfolio Manager, the Project Coordinator will be responsible for leading the Project Team in the day-to-day implementation of the country-level project activities and managing financial resources effectively and efficiently so as to achieve the Project Objective and Outcomes within the set timescale and available budget.

The Project Coordinator will work in close collaboration with the Programme, Operations, Communications and other project teams in the CO for effective achievement of results, anticipating and contributing to resolving complex programme/project-related issues and information delivery. S/he will ensure effective implementation of daily activities of the Project at the national level in compliance with appropriate UNDP policies and procedures.

The Project Coordinator will be responsible for implementation of in-country activities in accordance with the project document and approved work plan. The Project Coordinator for the Republic of Moldova is expected to closely cooperate with project counterparts, local authorities, partners, line ministries and regional authorities, and other relevant parties.

The role of National Project Coordinator will be to engage on day to day with the local governments, support technical assistance, knowledge exchange, capacity development, national level consultations and dialogues, support the implementation of the portfolio approach, launch and provide support in the implementation of the country level CFPs (Mayors for Economic Growth Annual Portfolio Call) & country-level sensemaking. Overall, the role of the country teams will be to support the implementation of the project, related administrative tasks and ensure consistency and complementarity with other programming.

With respect to overall coordination of in-country project activities the Project Coordinator is expected to:

ensure effective communication with national and local partners;
ensure timely preparation, update and implementation of project annual and detailed work plans, and other related documents for timely commencement of planned in-country activities and expected outputs;
organize and/or coordinate Project events;
supervise research activities and elaboration of joint knowledge products at the national level;
build partnerships with local authorities, relevant ministries, private sector and local actors;
coordinate implementation of the national component of the project in close cooperation with local authorities and other relevant parties;
